    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9540a33_71f67cc5",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-30T22:23:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Couldn\u0027t we add a `#define __ANDROID_API_V__ __ANDROID_API_FUTURE__` early on in the finalization process, so that people could start using `__ANDROID_API_V__` from the very beginning, and then change it to the finalized value when that\u0027s decided? Then we wouldn\u0027t have to pass in `__ANDROID_PLATFORM_API__`.\n\nAs is, wouldn\u0027t this cause issues for prebuilts or other apps with unique distribution methods? If you built an app before the V sdk was finalized, it would bake in the comparison against `__ANDROID_API_FUTURE__`, so then if you installed that old prebuilt on a newer phone it would start checking against a newer version than it should.",
      "revId": "02e9c714c5ba6d989e865b3adf3df6e66f291706",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9a25dcc_b0d63c11",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-30T23:29:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree, `#define __ANDROID_API_V__ __ANDROID_API_FUTURE__` could work. I think they wanted to use a concrete version numbers instead of 10000. Perhaps to support the case where two code names are under development. (with two different integers)..\n\n\n\u003e it would bake in the comparison against `__ANDROID_API_FUTURE__`\n\nI think this should be okay. `__builtin_available(android 10000,*)` becomes false on \"REL\" devices, which is what we want.",
      "parentUuid": "b9540a33_71f67cc5",
      "revId": "02e9c714c5ba6d989e865b3adf3df6e66f291706",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88dfd317_180f55bc",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-31T00:45:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e becomes false on \"REL\" devices, which is what we want.\n\nIsn\u0027t that a problem? You could take an app that was compiled on an old version, then run it on a newer device that is publicly released V, so we want the check to return true, not false.",
      "parentUuid": "b9a25dcc_b0d63c11",
      "revId": "02e9c714c5ba6d989e865b3adf3df6e66f291706",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "15681c61_1266d997",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-31T01:20:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh I see what you mean. So, for example, if a module built in in 24q2-release branch (sdk is still 34) is run on a V device (sdk is 35), you\u0027re saying the check should return true, right?\n\nHmm, that seeminly makes sense. But I don\u0027t think so. 24q1-release doesn\u0027t guarantee anything about 35 APIs. So, if a module is built in 24q1-release, it shouldn\u0027t call the new API even when it\u0027s run on a new platform.",
      "parentUuid": "88dfd317_180f55bc",
      "revId": "02e9c714c5ba6d989e865b3adf3df6e66f291706",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b9673c3a_7b380156",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-31T01:21:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I used 24q1-release or 24q2-release interchangeably as a REL platform but not V yet.",
      "parentUuid": "15681c61_1266d997",
      "revId": "02e9c714c5ba6d989e865b3adf3df6e66f291706",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5f57d3b_6786a45f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T19:52:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suppose `#define __ANDROID_API_V__ __ANDROID_API_FUTURE__` will have the same issue....\n\n\u003e I think they wanted to use a concrete version numbers instead of 10000\n\nWouldn\u0027t this solution also use 10000 until `__ANDROID_PLATFORM_API__ \u003e\u003d __ANDROID_API_V__`?",
      "parentUuid": "b9673c3a_7b380156",
      "revId": "02e9c714c5ba6d989e865b3adf3df6e66f291706",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ed95724f_40d19d59",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T20:07:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, this solution would pass 10000 to `__builtin_available` until `__ANDROID_PLATFORM_API__ \u003e\u003d __ANDROID_API_V__`.\n\nAgain, I agree that `#define __ANDROID_API_V__ __ANDROID_API_FUTURE__` would work just like suggestion in this CL. Especially for what I wanted to do. (guarding APIs). But `__ANDROID_API_V__` is already in use in many places as a concrete version (35). I\u0027m not sure I can change them all to work correctly.",
      "parentUuid": "c5f57d3b_6786a45f",
      "revId": "02e9c714c5ba6d989e865b3adf3df6e66f291706",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e87389f_8aec375b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T20:13:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "TBH, I think a better solution would be either\n- fix `__isOSVersionAtLeast()` to understand in-development version and evals to true with `__builtin_available(android __ANDROID_API_V__, *)`. Then we wouldn\u0027t need this CL. But I don\u0027t think it\u0027s feasible because `__isOSVersionAtLeast` is a clang implementation and we can\u0027t update it every year.\n- or, set `ro.build.version.sdk` to 35 even we\u0027re still developing V(35) in trunk_staging.",
      "parentUuid": "ed95724f_40d19d59",
      "revId": "02e9c714c5ba6d989e865b3adf3df6e66f291706",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "19df84e5_d9abcaed",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1535516
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T20:20:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess if the concern is about existing usages, could we add `#define AT_LEAST_V (__builtin_available(android __ANDROID_API_FUTURE__, *))` to `api-level.h` and update the finalizatin script to change it from `__ANDROID_API_FUTURE__` to `__ANDROID_API_V__` when finalizing?",
      "parentUuid": "1e87389f_8aec375b",
      "revId": "02e9c714c5ba6d989e865b3adf3df6e66f291706",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eeecf519_d4a65367",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-02T20:35:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, I\u0027m not familiar with how the finalization script works. I thought it\u0027s applied to the release branch after cut-off from the main. Will it work with Trunk Stable? AFAIK -next-/-trunk_staging- should work with the same code base. I\u0027m okay if it works as expected:\n- When platform sdk version is 34 and codename is VanillaIceCream (the current -trunk_staging-), then the guard should be true\n- When platform sdk version is 34 and codename is REL (the current -next-), then the guard should be false,\n- When platform sdk version is 35 and codename is REL, then the guard should be true\n..",
      "parentUuid": "19df84e5_d9abcaed",
      "revId": "02e9c714c5ba6d989e865b3adf3df6e66f291706",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
